{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CORRECTION-2BC7-B: one row of my audit table was wrong, and the correct value is more interesting\n\nIn AUDIT-2BC7-A I listed `test_mutation.py::_load_mutation` as an \"UNGUARDED overwrite\". **That is\nwrong.** I built that table by hand from an earlier string-based heuristic instead of from the AST\nwalk whose numbers I quoted alongside it. Re-derived properly, per function:\n\n```\nfile                                 func              registers?  shape\ntest_differ.py                       _load_module      yes         cache-first (name + __file__)\ntest_differ_conflict_resolution.py   _load_module      yes         cache-first (name + __file__)\ntest_differ_quarantine_suppression   _load_module      yes         cache-first (name + __file__)\ntest_differ_emits_probe.py           _load             yes         unconditional overwrite\ntest_apply_list_of_mutations.py      _load             yes         name-only cache, NO __file__ check\ntest_mutation.py                     _load_mutation    NO          UNREGISTERED private copy\ntest_differ.py (in-test loader)      test_diff_is_pure…NO          UNREGISTERED private copy (by design)\n```\n\n`_load_mutation` never touches `sys.modules` — it builds, execs and returns a module that is\n**registered nowhere**. So it cannot clobber another file's registration, which is what I accused it of.\n\n**Why the correct answer is worse to read than the wrong one.** \"Returns an unregistered copy of\n`mutation.py`\" is this ticket's own TITLE — it is the exact shape of the original defect. The\ndifference is only that `_load_mutation` reaches it deliberately and in isolation: nothing in\n`test_mutation.py` compares its objects against a class resolved out of `sys.modules`, so the two\ncopies never meet. It is safe by circumstance, not by construction. The moment a cell in that file\nasserts `isinstance(x, <registered> Mutation)` — or a helper it calls resolves the class cache-first,\nas `differ._load_mutation()` does — it reproduces 2bc7 exactly.\n\n`test_differ.py`'s in-test loader is a genuine by-design exception: it registers under the distinct\nname `mutation_for_diff_purity` precisely to get an isolated copy.\n\nSo the live unguarded registrants of the shared `\"mutation\"` key are **two**, not three:\n`test_differ_emits_probe.py::_load` (unconditional overwrite) and\n`test_apply_list_of_mutations.py::_load` (the name-only cache that\n`test_load_module_identity.py`'s docstring explicitly warns about — it can return a DIFFERENT file's\nmodule registered under the same key).\n\nThe rest of AUDIT-2BC7-A stands: zero real `setdefault` calls remain, 4 of 213 by-path loaders are\ncache-first, and the `outbound_differ` / `inbound_differ` / `reconcile` / `applier` keys have 9 / 8 / 4\n/ 3 registrants respectively with no cache-first loader among them."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785865968039577001,"uuid":"d5d33405-c7ca-41e1-adc1-49b38a9e7f5f"}